// screen.marco — asking what is on the screen, and never changing it.
//
// Every capability here READS. There is no sentence in this act that moves a pointer,
// presses a key, focuses a window or launches anything, and that is the whole point:
// a play uses this to decide whether its first line belongs on this stage, and
// deciding must not be doing.
//
// A host that cannot answer says so, and the play refuses. Silence is never yes.

the Screen is an act.
this exports Showing.   // ok if the screen the user named is the one in front
